2125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 1921 0 R
/T (I was not able to confirm a Swiss survey that directly assesses portrait vs. landscape preference. Given the heavy presence of smartphones in the Swiss market and the high volume of commute time, I would consider portrait / one-handed play as the default and landscape as the special cases, combat, or more enriched exploration. In the case of multilingual UI, it implies brief text, customizable button sizes, secure margins, and a language switch, which does not disrupt the design.)
/E (I was not able to confirm a Swiss survey that directly assesses portrait vs. landscape preference. Given the heavy presence of smartphones in the Swiss market and the high volume of commute time, I would consider portrait / one-handed play as the default and landscape as the special cases, combat, or more enriched exploration. In the case of multilingual UI, it implies brief text, customizable button sizes, secure margins, and a language switch, which does not disrupt the design.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
